Block 2: Ross 128, quick-look east component opposite in sign to the catalogue prediction (2026-11-15)

Reported (live quick look): east 1->2 pred +0.87 meas -1.68+-0.75; 1->3 +0.60 / -1.20+-0.79; 2->3 -0.26 / +0.47+-0.44; north agrees.

1) Sign error in the code? Not found.
   - Code read: site/src/quicklook.ts measureEpoch() and the prediction in QuickLookView.tsx both use east = (c - x) * 6.15 on the same grid (column 0 = east edge); worldToGrid/gridToWorld are inverses.
   - Evidence: logs/test_motion.log (same code, quick look vs full pipeline):
     Epsilon Indi B (unsaturated, east motion positive): all 6 pairs same sign as prediction and full pipeline, e.g. 0->1 pred +1.24, quick +0.99+-0.63, full +1.05+-0.06.
     WISE 0855 (east motion negative): 0->1 pred -3.49, quick -4.28+-1.63, full -3.02+-0.85.
     So the east sign is right in both directions.
   - NOT done: the comparison on LAWD 37 or SSSPM J1444-2019 asked for in the task. IRSA did not answer (see 3).

